Definitely not. As sjdevnull said, one excess tripe ration in inventory
after training the pet is enough. I'll admit that acquiring tripe when
playing with pacifist tactics is hard, since you'll let your pet take the
lead a lot, so it gets to the rations first. But try to make some effort to
collect tripe and you'll probably have a few rations quickly. Prepare a
shop, drop your starting capital inside, stand in the door and carefully
wait for the right moment to feed your treat, and your pet will multiply
your credit for you in no time. The effect lasts long enough to completely
empty a shop (including the cash) and sometimes even get a good start on a
second one (provided that you didn't make any compromises when feeding.
Just throw the ration at the turn that your pet has dropped something
exactly in front of you and hasn't moved away yet.)


